<title>CANADA: West Canada fertilizer shipment, inventory - Jly/Sep.</title>
<headline>West Canada fertilizer shipment, inventory - Jly/Sep.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Fertilizer Institute released its shipment and inventory data on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Western Canadian Fertilizer Shipments</p>
<p>	  July to September 1995 vs 1996</p>
<p>Fertilizer	  Prev Yr (94/95)  Cur Yr (95/96) Pct Change</p>
<p>UREA		    244,102 tonnes   293,517 tonnes +20.2</p>
<p>AMMONIUM SULPHATE    14,581	     18,298	  +25.5</p>
<p>AMMONIUM NITRATE     38,784	     53,457	  +37.8</p>
<p>ANHYDROUS AMMONIA    23,716	     25,234	   +6.4</p>
<p>OTHER*		    7,888		6,058	  -23.2</p>
<p>TOTAL:		  329,071	    396,564	  +20.5</p>
<p>Inventories on Sept 30, 1995 vs 1996</p>
<p>Fertilizer	  Sept 30, 1995    Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>UREA		    109,660	    124,030</p>
<p>AMMONIUM SULPHATE   103,492	    107,457</p>
<p>AMMONIUM NITRATE     46,479	     45,604</p>
<p>ANHYDROUS AMMONIA   286,777	    202,622</p>
<p>OTHER*		    9,923	     81,628</p>
<p>TOTAL:		  556,331	    561,341</p>
<p>*other includes other phosphates, sulphur solutions, elemental sulphur, sulphate and mixed fertilizer materials.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
